# 44. `List` vs `Sequence`

## List

Collection operations are generally eager.

```kotlin
val result = numbers
    .filter { it % 2 == 0 }
    .map { it * 10 }
```

The intermediate result is produced immediately.

---

## Sequence

Operations are lazy.

```kotlin
val result = numbers
    .asSequence()
    .filter { it % 2 == 0 }
    .map { it * 10 }
    .first()
```

Sequence processes elements progressively and can stop early when a terminal operation has enough information.

### Mental model

```text
List
→ eager

Sequence
→ lazy
```

Useful when:

* collections are large
* many operations are chained
* early termination is possible

